"[2610.08258] zkLLMPoT: Efficient Zero Knowledge Proof of Training for Large Language Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.08258)\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.08258\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 169\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 6 Oct 2026 (【5†v1】), last revised 11 Oct 2026 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:zkLLMPoT: Efficient Zero Knowledge Proof of Training for Large Language Models\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Junkai Liang】, 【7†Zhanpeng Guo】, 【8†Pengfei Wu】, 【9†Qingni Shen】, 【10†Jiaheng Zhang】, 【11†Zhonghai Wu】, 【12†Haiyang Xue】, 【13†Shengfang Zhai】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled zkLLMPoT: Efficient Zero Knowledge Proof of Training for Large Language Models, by Junkai Liang and 7 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【14†View PDF】 【15†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:Auditing the claimed outcomes of large language model (LLM) training is challenging when model weights and training data are private, while cryptographically proving the full training process is prohibitively expensive at Transformer scale. We present zkLLMPoT, a zero-knowledge framework that certifies auditor-defined properties of a trained checkpoint through forward evaluation rather than verification of its optimization trajectory.\nL17: zkLLMPoT includes 2 phases: 1) The trainer fixes the architecture and the model weights are committed. Then the auditor selects challenge sequences, preventing the trainer from modifying the checkpoint in response to the audit data. 2) Then the trainer proves the objective value attained by the committed model on those sequences. This formulation makes the certification cost independent of the number of training iterations, without revealing model weights or requiring access to private training data.\nL18: We build on sumcheck- and lookup-based arguments to certify Transformer computations, while supporting next-token loss and task-specific audit objectives. Across four model families, operator-level benchmarks yield proving times of 41-59 seconds for 1.1-1.5B-parameter models and 131 seconds at 13B for the covered operators, with verification below half a second at a sequence length of 512.\nL19: Comments:  | 18 pages, 4 figures, Preprint\nL20: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 94A60, 68T50\nL22: ACM (Association of Computing Machinery Classification) classes:  | E.3; I.2.6; I.2.7\nL23: Cite as:  | 【16†arXiv:2610.08258】 [cs.AI]\nL24:    | (or 【17†arXiv:2610.08258v2】 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL25:    | 【18†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2610.08258†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL26: ## Submission history\nL27: \nL28: From: Junkai Liang [【19†view email】]\nL29: 【5†[v1]】 Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:35:49 UTC (112 KB)\nL30: [v2] Sun, 11 Oct 2026 04:45:08 UTC (115 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled zkLLMPoT: Efficient Zero Knowledge Proof of Training for Large Language Models, by Junkai Liang and 7 other authors\nL37: \nL38:   * 【14†View PDF】\nL39:   * 【15†HTML (experimental)】\nL40:   * 【20†TeX Source】\nL41: \nL42: 【21†view license】\nL43: \nL44: ### Additional Features\nL45: \nL46:   * 【22†Audio Summary】\nL47: ### Current browse context:\nL48: \nL49: cs.AI\nL50: \nL51: 【23†< prev】   |   【24†next >】\nL52: \nL53: 【25†new】 | 【26†recent】 | 【27†2026-10】\nL54: \nL55: Change to browse by:\nL56: \nL57: 【28†cs】\nL58: \nL59: ### References & Citations\nL60: \nL61:   * 【29†SciX†scixplorer.org】\nL62:   * 【30†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL63:   * 【31†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL64: \nL65: [Button: export BibTeX 